  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "capture: Always pass the interface description to the capture child",
  "description": "Interfaces are passed from Wireshark or tshark to dumpcap using the\nname, which avoids having to retrieve the interface list. We already\npass the description for extcaps; pass it for other interfaces as well\nto put in the IDB and use for the filename.\n\nThis make captures spawned from Wireshark or tshark have the same\ninterface description and same tempfile name as when running dumpcap\ndirectly. It particularly affects captures using the loopback interface,\non both Windows (where a Win32 API call cannot retrieve the Loopback\ninterface description) and other OSes.\n\nFix #18466",
